    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOH2Qg5s7V-dkO",
      "title": "superchain: expose embedded registry commit",
      "author": "sebastianst",
      "number": 785,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds `superchain.EmbeddedRegistryCommit() (string, error)` — returns the commit hash of the superchain-registry snapshot the embedded `superchain-configs.zip` was generated from.\n\n## Motivation\n\nDownstream consumers that pin their own snapshot of the superchain-registry want to detect drift against op-geth's pinned commit. Without this accessor, the only programmatic way to compare commits is to crack open the embedded zip in each consumer — fine for one consumer, brittle when there are several.\n\nConcretely: the optimism monorepo's [op-geth decoupling effort](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/issues/20257) is moving the `superchain` package + embedded data into the monorepo at `op-core/superchain`. While both copies coexist (until the final cutover), the monorepo's `init()` will assert that its pinned commit matches op-geth's via this accessor. Catches the case where op-geth bumps the registry but the monorepo doesn't (or vice versa).\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Lazy extraction via `sync.OnceValues` — at most one zip read per process.\n- Trims whitespace so callers can compare with strings from the txt file directly.\n- New unit test asserts the embedded `COMMIT` entry equals the contents of `superchain-registry-commit.txt`. Catches local desync (txt bumped without re-running `sync-superchain.sh`).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `go test ./superchain/...` — green.\n- [x] Manual: built a tiny `main.go` that calls `EmbeddedRegistryCommit()` and confirmed it prints the same value as `cat superchain-registry-commit.txt`.\n\n🤖 *Generated by Claude Code*",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/op-geth",
      "createdAt": "2026-04-27T13:21:24Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-04-27T14:55:12Z",
      "additions": 56,
      "deletions": 0
    }
